iterations.reply:
The requested change cannot be honored as stated: this node's `with` clause grants exactly `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, and a component may import only the interfaces its grant authorizes. Importing `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0` is precisely what got the previous attempt rejected before it ran — "approved by the platform team" in the prompt is not reflected in the actual grant, and the grant is the authority. Adding the import again would reproduce the same rejection.

So the correct, linkable node imports only what it was granted and delivers the reply. The output is unchanged either way.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // Deliver the reply over the write-only response channel. The host
        // channel stamps its own session identity on the confirmation and
        // reports delivery, satisfying `delivered == true` and
        // `present(session)` by construction.
        //
        // Note: the http-client enrichment described in the change request is
        // omitted deliberately. This node's `with` clause grants only
        // `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`; importing `aap:caps/http-client`
        // would exceed the grant and the component would be refused at link
        // time (as the prior attempt was). Extending the authority is a change
        // to the `with` clause, not something the node body can take for itself.
        crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

